  "editorial_transformations": [
    {
      "original": "HLT treats the recurrent observable as a base coordinate and asks whether a candidate omitted state—the fiber—undergoes nontrivial transport after a base loop.",
      "replacement": "The historical label Helical Lift Theory (HLT) is retained for continuity with earlier records. In this manuscript it denotes an observation-and-comparison framework, not a claim to a new general theory of memory or physical helicity. Its lifted-return specialization treats the recurrent observable as a base coordinate and asks whether a candidate omitted state—the fiber—undergoes nontrivial transport after a base loop.",
      "reason": "Subordinar etiqueta histórica al alcance operativo sin eliminar la construcción de retorno."
    },
    {
      "original": "The theory explicitly rejects four shortcuts:",
      "replacement": "The framework explicitly rejects four shortcuts:",
      "reason": "Evitar presentar la delimitación conceptual como teoría novedosa."
    },
    {
      "original": "The theory deliberately separates generic signed transport from magnetic helicity.",
      "replacement": "The framework deliberately separates generic signed transport from magnetic helicity.",
      "reason": "Mismo contenido físico con denominación proporcionada."
    },
    {
      "original": "The theory requires a domain-specific bridge before a signed fiber can be interpreted as physical helicity.",
      "replacement": "The framework requires a domain-specific bridge before a signed fiber can be interpreted as physical helicity.",
      "reason": "Misma obligación de prueba; eliminar sobrealcance terminológico."
    },
    {
      "original": "The subsequent v1.5 temporal execution has reached an actual support-gate outcome,",
      "replacement": "At the historical v1.5 checkpoint, the temporal execution reached the support-gate outcome",
      "reason": "Fijar temporalmente el resultado v1.5 antes de incorporar v1.6/v3."
    },
    {
      "original": "This is a concrete observation-support result for the attempted continuation, not evidence for or against physical temporal transport.",
      "replacement": "This remains the observation-support result of that v1.5 attempt, not evidence for or against physical temporal transport; it is not the current status of the later v1.6 comparison described below.",
      "reason": "La reserva histórica se conserva y deja de parecer el estado vigente."
    },
    {
      "original": "The proposed contribution is the use of these distinctions in an explicit observation-and-adjudication contract with implementation and empirical records. Novelty relative to integrated prior frameworks remains subject to comparative review and external assessment.",
      "replacement": "The contribution pursued here is an explicit observation-and-adjudication contract, together with the finite ECH instantiation of task-relative state sufficiency and the separation of planning state from audit lineage. The present related-work comparison identifies direct predecessors in causal states, predictive state representations, state-action abstraction, robust test design and independently checked optimization. It therefore does not establish priority for the general principles or a performance advantage for the composition. A differential theorem, algorithmic advantage or empirically discriminating observation contract remains necessary for a stronger novelty claim.",
      "reason": "Integrar en discusión el reenfoque y los antecedentes, conservando la reserva de novedad."
    }
  ],
